AB  - Wandering spleen is a rare condition resulting from the absence or looseness of the hanging ligaments that keep the spleen in its normal anatomical location. It can lead to an acute abdomen with torsion and infarction of the splenic pedicle. In this article, we present a patient who came to the hospital with a grievance of severe abdominal pain and was diagnosed with wandering spleen torsion. The patient was treated with splenopexy. Although it is rare, a wandering spleen should be considered in the differential diagnosis of acute abdomen.
