AB  - Splenic necrosis is extremely rare in neonates, the cases recorded so far being secondary to torsion of wandering organs.
   A newborn with an abdominal mass who underwent exchange transfusions through an umbilical catheter is presented here. Comprehensive investigation led to the suspicion of enteric duplication, but a splenic necrosis with no features of wandering spleen was found at laparotomy.
   The pathogenesis and preoperative diagnostic work-up of splenic necrosis are emphasised.
