AB  - A once ignored and often removed organ, the spleen has come to be viewed with greater respect given our more sophisticated understanding of its important immune functions. Although splenic emergencies including infarction, rupture, and abscess are less common than other pediatric abdominal emergencies, their accurate recognition is important for potential splenic preservation. The relative role of cross-sectional imaging in guiding therapeutic decisions in these emergent conditions is discussed.
